Subject: Adds compact opcodes for `load_i8` and `move`

What this does
  Adds compact opcodes for `load_i8` and `move`.

Why we need it
  These frequent instructions carry register indices as two bytes even though the functions fit in the narrow range.

What it adds
  Adds one-byte register forms with per-opcode selection and keeps the existing wide forms when an index does not fit.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  Yes. The register blobs are regenerated in 9999. `BC_VERSION` is unchanged.
